            <ArticleTitle>Serotonergic influence on cholinergic-induced analgesia: differences in two inbred strains of mice.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>347-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>C57BL/6 (C57) and DBA/2 (DBA) inbred mice showed different analgesic responses to cholinergic stimulation. The simultaneous administration of muscarinic and serotonergic agonists, oxotremorine and 5-methoxy-NN-dimethyltryptamine (5-MeODMT), lowered the antinociceptive effect of the cholinergic drug in DBA mice, while no effects were detectable in the C57 strain. These results suggest a strain-dependent behavioural effect of the interaction of cholinergic and serotonergic neuronal systems.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
